  "_comment": "A lap round and through a volcano's crater. The rim straight with no wall on the crater side, a 22 degree banked sweeper along the rim, then the Heave: the drop into the caldera over crust that swells in travelling waves. On the floor, 55 m of dash straight into the Loop: 13 m of radius, upside down over the lava lake, out 20 m to the right. Round into the Smelter, a tunnel where three cooling presses stamp the road in turn and a slag belt shoves karts at the wall, a crucible swinging across its mouth, a dash panel and the Pour: a glide over the lava river onto the lower terrace and straight into the second loop. Then the crater wall: a 65 degree grip bank climbing out of the pit, the long climb back to the rim, a trick ramp over the lip and home under the rim road's bridge over the loop straight. The crust hop cuts the sweeper over off-road crust (worth it with a mushroom), the lava tube drains and opens on lap 2, the river under the Pour surges every 14 s (a dash strip on the landing), and on lap 3 the floor cracks: lava along the outer lanes of the loop straight.",
